{
  "slug": "artist:dj-premier",
  "name": "DJ Premier",
  "editorial_article": "Born Christopher Edward Martin in 1966 and raised in Brooklyn, this Houston native defined the New York boom-bap sound through his work with Gang Starr alongside rapper Guru. His production method relies heavily on sampling jazz, funk, and soul, famously chopping records—including previous works by artists he is currently producing—to construct new arrangements. Premier's technical skill extends to scratching, where he utilizes an encyclopedic memory of hip-hop lyrics to manipulate vocal samples into entirely new hooks. Beyond his foundational work with the Gang Starr Foundation and artists like M.O.P. and Jeru the Damaja, he has reached mainstream audiences through chart-topping collaborations, including Christina Aguilera's 2006 single Ain't No Other Man. He founded Year Round Records in 2010 and later formed the duo PRhyme with Royce da 5'9\" in 2014, continuing to curate hip-hop production across generations.",
